  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-09T14:40:03.156Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Udon and Udonsharp will make world more interactable and active games will also possible compared to SDK2 with much deeper effects, store values and refresh world content.\nBut when i program Video lesson boards with UdonSharp, it works good in PC world. Even some special Udon counters works good in PC.\nBut at Quest side...\nThe Lesson boards doesn't work well, some special Udon counters doesn't work well.\nThis is not supposed to make (huge) differences between PC and Quest.\n\nEspecially i have no Quest headset, am i force to buy one for only testing purposes? Come on, why should i buy Quest headset only for that? This should done better, seriously.\n\nSo dear Udon developers, make Quest better for Udon scripting. This will reduce stress on world creators, especially game creators, to make it right at Quest world. Or you must make good alternatives between PC and Quest, then we need special wiki site for PC-Quest Udon coding, with some limits and some workarounds. That will make us less troublesome with Udon coding for Quest side.\n\nWithout that, i have no enough knownledge to find correct solutions and so i am stuck. So, you must do something to make testing worlds in Quest easier, or give special toolkit for better debugging in Unity.\n\nBecause, without some equity, it's stupid to make strange or less great alternatives for Quest. Why make double work? Udon script must work on both sides without much problems. Sure Quest cannot do everything, but it still can do something but it's not working well. Refreshing boards is a problem on Quest.\nAlso help UdonSharp creator to make it better for Quest.\n\nThank you very much.",
